          "30000156 / OWR-768-006: Limiting Cycle Distributions of Birational Maps",
          "",
          "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23539734",
          "A fixed birational map without a prime-field cycle-distribution limit \u2014 Alec Kriebel (ORCID 0009-0001-9320-500X), v1.1 (2026-10-21). Unrefereed preprint. Fixed L(u,v)=(u,(u\u00b2+1)v) permutes the full affine plane for p\u22613 mod4; point-weighted periods normalized by p have, at each fixed 1/2\u2264x<1, CDF 1\u2212\u03c6(p\u22121)/(p\u22121)+o(1), limsup 1 and liminf at most 23/24. Neither those CDF values nor the period measures converge on any admissible prime subset of positive upper relative density. A separate all-odd-prime proposition treats the regular domain p(p-r), r=0 or2, and uniform-point exceptional-fiber deletion or arbitrary finite nonnegative assigned periods only there. Bounded statistics change by O(1/p); no positive-upper-prime-density selection restores convergence under these conventions. Completed measures lie on nonnegative reals; assigned periods may exceed p. The triangular family, primitive quadratic values, shifted-prime totient mean and continuous scalar law are established and credited; this is a scoped application to Vivaldi\u2019s 2004 broad existence assertion (joint work with Roberts). No new map family, character-sum theorem, arithmetic mean/scalar law, universal elliptic, polynomial-automorphism or prime-average cycle theorem claimed. Bounded priority audit found no authenticated exact earlier application in inspected sources; the cited Neum\u00e4rker\u2013Roberts\u2013Viallet\u2013Vivaldi 2011 preprint body/version relationships remain unrecovered. No worldwide novelty, current-open status or historical firstness claim. PDF and editable-source/verification ZIP preserve all 17 original files and historical audits; new dependency-free checker supports finite computations, while the proof uses cited classical inputs. Extensive AI use in research, model/proof development, computation, literature investigation, writing and adversarial verification. No formal independent human peer review; internal AI audits are not human peer review. Primary source: https://webspace.maths.qmul.ac.uk/f.vivaldi/research/Oberwolfach.pdf. Record: https://zenodo.org/records/23539734. PR: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/280."
        ]
      },
      "root_files": [
        {
